    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0349" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/6–1545:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-15T18:00:00+02:00">June 15, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 15—5:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3595. Mytel 3572, June 15.<anchor n="46" xml:id="d284-f1"/> In view of the fact
                    that Bidault told me last night that instructions had been sent to Massigli
                    agreeing to our suggestions for the French occupation zone the change suggested
                        <pb facs="0350" n="340" xml:id="pg340"/> in Murphy’s 3543, June 14 would
                    have the most lamentable effect on the French at this juncture.<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d284-f2"/> Copy given to Murphy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d284-f1" n="46" xml:id="d284-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; in it Ambassador Caffery reported that Foreign Minister Bidault had
                    told him on the night of June 14 that the necessary instructions had been sent
                    to Ambassador Massigli agreeing to the U.S. suggestions for the French
                    occupation zone (740.00119 Control (Germany)/6–1545).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d284-f2" n="47" xml:id="d284-f2-content">
                <p>The Department replied in telegram 2782, June 16, 3 p.m., as follows: “The
                    Department completely agrees with you.” (740.00119 Control (Germany)/6–1545)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
